            "review_title": "Review at Le Royal Saigon",
            "review_text": "Darth8r\nCypress78 contributions\n0\nBe prepared with this one!\nFeb 2018 • Solo\nI stayed at the Majestic where this restaurant is located. It is VERY ornate and fancy, the servers dressed in gorgeous garbs. I actually was looking for the restaurant described in my in-room guide to the hotel that was described as 'traditional Vietnamese food' and I mistakenly ended up at Le Royal. I was dressed in ordinary street clothes not expecting the elegance of this place. The servers were giddy; they treated me like they were shocked I was there. The place is quite large, and there wasn't another soul in there at dinner time on a Thursday evening, which I found odd. The prices were quite high compared to what I had become accustomed to in VN. I chose a duck breast dish and the server was persistent in having me choose other dishes as well; I wasn't that hungry so I kept with my order. When it was served, I was shocked to find two pieces of duck breast about the size each of an eraser; at best, two bites for each. Both had a thick layer of fat on them. Accompanying them were three small balls of rice and two baby carrots. Of course I realized then that this is a multi-course type restaurant where you would typically spend a couple million dong and make an event of it. The whole thing was rather bizarre. And during my 4 day stay, I never once saw a customer inside, just the staff in the opening lobby peering out the window looking very bored. Live and learn!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 25, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
